{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/105468-first-time-scion-st-tips","id":105468,"title":"First time Scion ST - Tips?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-04-04T03:18:10-07:00","id":105468,"title":"First time Scion ST - Tips?","content":"So, somehow I've ended up being chosen to run a game of Scion for a new group. What's worrying is that I've never played it before, let alone run it. I'm willing to give it a shot (the group knows and they seem ok with it, I get the impression they haven't played it before either), any tips?<br /> <br /> I know Epic Dex is broken: I'm going to suggest a houserule to somewhat address that (namely, that melee attacks can be made using Strength or Dexterity for hitting. I know it's imperfect, but it's simple), I know the game kind of falls down past Hero (thankfully I'll be keeping it to Hero tier). Any suggestions or tips beyond that?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-04T04:34:56-07:00","id":105488,"title":"","content":"Look through the houserule and fan material sticky at the top of the forum.<br /> Go over to Gotham By Night.<br /> Don't be afraid to chuck the rules if you've got a feel for the scene.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1011-phgraves","name":"PHGraves","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1011_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-04T05:28:52-07:00","id":105517,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Allan53</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/105468-first-time-scion-st-tips#post105468\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I know Epic Dex is broken: I'm going to suggest a houserule to somewhat address that (namely, that melee attacks can be made using Strength or Dexterity for hitting. I know it's imperfect, but it's simple)</div> </div> </div> </div>Place I play at has a perfect little knack for this called Between the Ribs, if you've played NWoD think of it like the merit Fighting Finesse, in that it allows you to use the precision (Hope I spelled that right, kinda tired) strikes to deal damage as opposed to the strength behind the blow. They charge 1 Legend per use (If I remember right) but since this'll be your game you can keep or chuck the cost.<br /> <br /> As far as other advice, test the waters first when it comes to throwing something at your group, get a feel for what they can handle. If they're a primarily mental group give them something simple to figure out first to see if they can actually figure it out than work your way up from there, if they're a physical group pick a Titanspawn out of the book, throw it at them and see what kind of damage they can do. <br /> <br /> Also on the note for physical players, some advice I wish others I play under would listen to. The goal for scion is not to give them some godawful powerful monster that they have to work as a group to defeat, it really takes away the feel of epic awesomeness when every victory is a &quot;Just Barely&quot; when it is a group fighting against one thing. Throw smaller things at them and throw it at them in bulk so when they take injuries it is because they had a lot of shit thrown at them and they managed to stomp the shit out of them.....it is somehow more awesome when you manage to crush a bunch of things and come out with some injuries, than it is to have a bunch of folks team up on one thing and just barely kill it even if it doesn't lay a finger on you. <br /> <br /> When it does come time to throw the &quot;Big Bad&quot; at them remember be descriptive. If someone happens to land a blow that just rocks the fuck out of them and this happens to be someone who has a healing knack DO NOT just describe it as &quot;He heals it up almost as quickly as you hit him&quot; nothing has pissed me off more, than seeing that weak ass post response when I manage to lay some serious hurting on a thing. Give a description of how badly the guy got injured, if the player damned near put his foot through the guys chest let them know it, describe the sickening bone crunch of his rib cage crushing under his foot, the meaty tearing of the flesh and organs as those same ribs escort the foot into the fools chest and the sick suction sound as he pulls his foot out while the creature falls to its knees in pain, barely holding on to that last thread of its life just before its flesh starts to mend itself back up, the cracks in its hard chitinous shell seeming to seal back together while the monster stands and spits out a gob of blood. <br /> <br /> Scion is a game that focuses a LOT on cinematic, hell they have a system in place for how awesome your description of an attack is (Stunt Dice).<br /> <br /> I may be focusing a lot on the combat aspect but it is mostly because I know from starting games with new players that while you won't always have a Machiavellian Manipulator or a Steven Hawkings genius in the group, you'll almost always have someone who can beat some ass.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'll be your Huckleberry","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2397-the-dude","name":"The Dude","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-04T15:20:30-07:00","id":105863,"title":"","content":"I'll certainly make a note of that, I have played NWoD and Exalted, so I'm familiar with the notion of stunting and Fighting Finesse.<br /> <br /> Although, doesn't Scion use Dex (and thus Epic Dex) as an attacking attribute anyway? And making them able to use Dex on damage as well, wouldn't that just overload Epic Dex even more than it already is? From what I understand, the current situation is that if you use EDex, you'll likely get extra successes, but at least it'll be mitigated by DV and suchforth, while EStr doesn't have that drawback, which goes a little way to balancing them (not enough, from what I've been told, but it's something). Or are you suggesting using Strength for melee attacks by standard, and needing this knack for using Dex?<br /> <br /> And I'll be sure to make the descriptions appropriately awesome. The Big Bad will be a challenging fight, but I see the challenge with him being more 'can you find him' and 'what is he doing' then 'OMG this guy can hit us with a battleship'. The fact that combat optimisation isn't a strong point of mine somewhat helps that decision <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-04T18:53:11-07:00","id":105963,"title":"","content":"There is another knack used called The Beast Within that will allow you to attack with strength, basically the reverse of the other knack. Either way the &quot;Attack&quot; attribute will be an issue only if you allow it to be. I've never seen much of an issue with Dexterity and not sure how folks see it as &quot;Broken&quot; so I can't really be all that helpful with issues solving it. Damage rolls face the same problem attack rolls do, since you still have to beat a set trait, just, instead of DV you have to beat their soak.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'll be your Huckleberry","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2397-the-dude","name":"The Dude","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-04T23:53:45-07:00","id":106078,"title":"","content":"Dexterity is considered broken because it does double duty. It provides both attack and defense. Instead of just determining if you hit, it also determines how HARD you hit. Strength is useless without Dexterity and while Stamina can provide soak, it's generally better not to get hit at all. So Dexterity does both attack <i>and</i> defense, but also does those things <i>better</i> than the Attributes that can <i>only</i> perform either one or the other. Strength can't be used to avoid damage, and Stamina can't be used to inflict it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-05T00:08:20-07:00","id":106084,"title":"","content":"As I understand it, the issue is that a character with EDex in combat will just about always beat a character without, due to its large influence on both DV and attack (and thus damage, albeit to a lesser extent than EStr). And since many antagonists have EDex, it's kind of necessary for a character, which impairs character concept/mechanical alignment.<br /> <br /> Near I can tell, anyway. Never having played it, I'm running off reading of the rules and what other people have said.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-05T07:02:14-07:00","id":106251,"title":"","content":"I try to encourage my players to work out the details of what they want to become and figure out what it takes to get there. It helps keep the players away from min maxing and focused on developing the character that fits the Legend they want to tell. If the players actually do this I find that it takes a lot of stress off the ST as most of the issues with Scion as the result of pushing the system to its limits or dramatic differences is character power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/151-hark","name":"Hark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar151_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"932"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-05T07:09:19-07:00","id":106255,"title":"","content":"Epic Dexterity can be coutered by Epic social's Knacks (any Knack that can make a target still is efficient enough to make Epic Dex useless), Pesedjet's and Loa's PSP Boons, Chaos, Sun, Moon, and so on...<br /> <br /> My feelings about Scion 1\u00b0 are very positives. I always enjoyed GM-ing, even at demigod level I didn't have all the issues everyone's talking about. I DO understand them but not every player will do that. Maybe antagonists might be created that way... so what? Change them so that your players get a chance. You play hidden behind a &quot;wall&quot; that allows you to cheat.. Epic Dex is nothing compared to your power over the game.<br /> <br /> If most of the issues start at demigod level, then you won't have to worry for now. Start playing the game with the rules you like the most -even the real rules are okay- and see how will that affect your players and yourself.<br /> <br /> I enjoy playing Scion but less than GM-ing it. It's just a game. Don't put too much pressure on yourself and on your players. Play it first, and see for youself.<br /> <br /> Edit: Hark got a very good point on this (just saw that you posted)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1837-wickedgrail","name":"Wickedgrail","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1837_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-05T07:45:10-07:00","id":106264,"title":"","content":"It's worth noting that Epic Dexterity isn't the only way to be an effective combatant. Strength can be used for attack rolls in a grapple, and strengths grappling knacks are about the most devestating attacks in the game. The Intelligence Knack Fight With Your Head from Ragnarok make Epic Intelligence a viable mode of combat, though is pretty broken when combined with other modes of combat. I want to say that there are some boons out there that are combat effective when coupled with appropriate Epic Attributes, but I can't remember any off the top of my head.<br /> <br /> Every time I run a Scion game I go look up other peoples house rules. There are a lot of good ones that help to deal with issues that the game has. I haven't played the game RAW since the for campaign I played in.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/151-hark","name":"Hark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar151_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"932"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-05T08:36:36-07:00","id":106292,"title":"","content":"Ehhh.... I think a games rules should be playable without having to be significantly tweaked out of the box. Sure, there will always be glitches and attendant tweaks, but the usual problems with Dex in almost all White Wolf games are magnified in Scion with the Epics. <br /> <br /> Telgar is right. The problem with Dex is that it does attack, defense and damage. It's defense is better than Stamina. Strength may be better for damage, but, unless it's a Clinch, if you don't hit (Dex) it doesn't matter how much potential you have. You can't get away from it. Dex is THE combat stat and, if you want to try to jury-rig other stats to fulfill it, you will be devoting a lot of character buys to be even (really slightly behind) a character who is just buying Epic Dex. And that character? She's taking Dex Knacks that are making her Dex even more effective.<br /> <br /> I know there are a lot of house rules out there as fixes. I'm using a few of them in the game I'm running. I have an overlap of those and some others in the game I'm playing. Still not satisfied. If anyone starts buying into Dex heavily for combat purposes, I'll just start running and hiding. And in my game, the Dex fighter is 1. broken b/c of some bad decisions on my part and 2. MUCH MUCH better at fighting than the Str based fighter, who is supposed to be the band's designated heavy. (She's got some social skills as their &quot;bad cop&quot;. He just puts things down.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-05T09:59:14-07:00","id":106340,"title":"","content":"Enemies with Epic stamina can readily ignore a guy with nothing but epic dex giving strength guys something to bash on. Epic dex is by far the best stat, but doesn't work on its own.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/151-hark","name":"Hark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar151_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"932"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-05T12:31:21-07:00","id":106445,"title":"","content":"It's true Epic Dex doesn't work on it's own, but it's far more valuable statistically than either Strength or Stamina. Clinches may offer a way to fight without Epic Dex, but you then lose out on the ability to have <i>weapons</i>. And weapons are kinda important in Scion, because of Speed. Which is a whole other issue. Basically, the combat system in Scion is terrible.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-05T12:54:19-07:00","id":106457,"title":"","content":"You're right, but to be fair, pretty much everything mechanical about Scion is terrible.<br /> <br /> Also a clinch takes away your opponents dv, allowing the rest of the group to beat it senseless too. There is some give and take going on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/151-hark","name":"Hark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar151_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"932"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-05T15:19:41-07:00","id":106557,"title":"","content":"Ok, the take-away I'm getting here is to just run with the system RAW, and tweak as need be depending on how the group goes? Coolio (assuming they're OK with the rules potentially changing halfway through, albeit through discussion of course). That way if it becomes a problem, it can be fixed, and if not, well, no need to fix.<br /> <br /> I don't see combat being a huge part of this game, so any potential flaws shouldn't really ruin things. Apart from that, do my usual and let the mechanics work when they do, avoid them when unnecessary, and fix them when they are necessary but don't work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-05T15:32:38-07:00","id":106561,"title":"","content":"My group are all experienced people. When I told them that A) I have not ST'ed in awhile and was using this chronicle to get my legs under me and B) The rules are not the best and they will be fluid, then they were surprisingly amenable with both and instead of hating the changes I make, they come back with positive feedback and have helped me tweak it. They love the stories. They love the roleplay. We just are all working together to make the game work.<br /> In short, make sure that they know ahead of time and to jot down notes on rules they think can be tweaked. Then discuss it between games and get input from everyone. This will work to make sure that the game is tweaked to perfection for your group and styles.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/786-thedonnie","name":"thedonnie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-05T18:23:42-07:00","id":106641,"title":"","content":"Yeah, these guys seem pretty cool. Little worried because I don't know them very well, and I've never gamed with them before, but most gamers are pretty cool as long as you're up-front, and I have been, so that works out ok.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-06T00:13:50-07:00","id":106764,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Allan53</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/105468-first-time-scion-st-tips?p=106557#post106557\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, the take-away I'm getting here is to just run with the system RAW, and tweak as need be depending on how the group goes? Coolio (assuming they're OK with the rules potentially changing halfway through, albeit through discussion of course).</div> </div> </div> </div>God if only more ST's where like this, I sometimes get tired of dealing with an ST who likes to change up the rules of the game out of nowhere, doesn't discuss it with any of the players who actually have to deal with the changes most of the time, bitches that the players are &quot;Whining&quot; when it does get discussed and people make it clear that they don't like it, and uses that as an indicator that they're clearly the victim of selfish players and changes the rules anyways...than of course whines when people leave the game unable to understand why.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'll be your Huckleberry","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2397-the-dude","name":"The Dude","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-06T08:55:26-07:00","id":106924,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Allan53</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/105468-first-time-scion-st-tips?p=106557#post106557\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, the take-away I'm getting here is to just run with the system RAW, and tweak as need be depending on how the group goes? Coolio (assuming they're OK with the rules potentially changing halfway through, albeit through discussion of course). That way if it becomes a problem, it can be fixed, and if not, well, no need to fix.<br /> <br /> I don't see combat being a huge part of this game, so any potential flaws shouldn't really ruin things. Apart from that, do my usual and let the mechanics work when they do, avoid them when unnecessary, and fix them when they are necessary but don't work.</div> </div> </div> </div>For a first-time ST, I would recommend going with RAW even as broken and hilariously patched as it is. As the game continues and you find need to adjust/tweak, then sit down with your players and go over the ideas. While I've long since left Scion RAW (I now use the unofficial Scion 2.0 google document) we still tweak and adjust rules depending on things that happen in play. After every tweak, or before it, the players are consulted. <br /> <br /> However, Scion's social system is horribly flawed as well, so expect tweaks there after the players first turn their powers on the band, or try to convince their fellows.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/606-aynie","name":"Aynie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar606_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-07T06:39:49-07:00","id":107409,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Dude</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/105468-first-time-scion-st-tips?p=106764#post106764\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> God if only more ST's where like this, I sometimes get tired of dealing with an ST who likes to change up the rules of the game out of nowhere, doesn't discuss it with any of the players who actually have to deal with the changes most of the time, bitches that the players are &quot;Whining&quot; when it does get discussed and people make it clear that they don't like it, and uses that as an indicator that they're clearly the victim of selfish players and changes the rules anyways...than of course whines when people leave the game unable to understand why.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I've played under that type. It's...terrible. I've certainly got my faults as an ST, but I can say with a fair degree of certainty that I don't just drop things on people from on high. Can't really understand why STs would run like that (I speak figuratively of course, I've got a good idea why actually), just ends up being not fun for everyone, and why would you bother going to all the effort of STing if it's not going to be fun?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-12T07:52:12-07:00","id":111471,"title":"","content":"Yeah, control freak comes to mind as to the &quot;Why&quot; and I know my faults as an ST and that is that I'm a bit to much of an Asshole. I can be a very understanding and helpful individual when I'm talking to a new player, or a player asks me an honest question about something that they're just not getting. But when I get dumbass submissions or dumbass questions they make my eye twitch and I sorta wanna smack them, and I tend to loose patience<br /> <br /> Example of Dumbass Submission: A Werewolf: The Apocalypse character - Kinfolk of Tribe Silver Fang and a Private Investigator - Relevant Stats: Appearance: 4, Perception: 2, Pure Breed: 5, Investigation: 0, Law: 0..........yes he made a cyber-bunny and couldn't even manage to put a single dot in a relevant skill and even his mental attributes were his lowest grouping of attributes. <br /> <br /> Example of a Dumbass Question: My werewolf is meditating on the top of the local mountain, he's been out there for 3 days...what is he thinking?<br /> <br /> Both of those things caused me to go from understanding ST to the guy who insults you for being so stupid that it causes me to want to perform a late term abortion on you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'll be your Huckleberry","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2397-the-dude","name":"The Dude","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-21T02:58:31-07:00","id":116869,"title":"","content":"I only recently started STing a Scion game with a couple of my long time nWoD players. since this is also my first Scion game, I've been testing the waters a lot and experimenting with new GMing styles. My players are used to me tweaking the rules and I've never done so without telling them why (such as my house rule on the difference between Armor and Defense in nWoD).<br /> <br /> My players have since fought and killed two fenrir, a handful of werewolves, and some giants. The group consists of two players with two characters each. One plays a couple of combat characters (with their own focuses, so they aren't simply copies of each other), the other plays a medic and a sniper. Combat wise, the group works really well together. I let the sniper bypass armor provided he takes an aimed shot (he's taken to aiming straight for the eyes now). The two main fighters are unfortunately focusing heavily on clinches when I know that the player would at the very least like her Scion of the Monkey King use his staff.<br /> <br /> As for Legend, I did some math based on stuff I've seen in the books and told my players their Legend will increase when they complete a number of stories equal to their next dot of Legend, but that I may change this depending on various circumstances.<br /> <br /> I've also house ruled that Hardness subtracts from raw damage rather than gets compared to it since it seemed useless when practically every character I've seen can easily beat the hardness granted by the medic's Aegis boon and also many of the numbers I see in <i>Scion: Hero</i>.<br /> <br /> Is there anything else I should note, change, and let my players know about before I spend 5 minutes or more muttering to myself &quot;that doesn't seem right/fair&quot;?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1545,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1545-aodhstormeyes","user":"aodhstormeyes","date":". 04-21-2014, 06:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1545-aodhstormeyes","name":"aodhstormeyes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}